    "text": "A charged particle is introduced at the origin <math><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>&#160;</mi><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>&#160;</mi><mi>z</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math> with a given initial velocity <math><mover accent=\"true\"><mrow><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover></math> . A uniform electric field <math><mover accent=\"true\"><mrow><mi>E</mi></mrow><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover><mi>&#160;</mi></math> and a uniform magnetic field <math><mover accent=\"true\"><mrow><mi>B</mi></mrow><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover></math> exist everywhere. The velocity <math><mover accent=\"true\"><mrow><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover></math> , electric field <math><mover accent=\"true\"><mrow><mi>E</mi></mrow><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover><mi>&#160;</mi></math> and a uniform magnetic field <math><mover accent=\"true\"><mrow><mi>B</mi></mrow><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover></math> are given in the columns below<table border=\"1\">\t<tbody>\t\t<tr>\t\t\t<td>Column 1</td>\t\t\t<td>Column 2</td>\t\t\t<td>Column 3</td>\t\t</tr>\t\t<tr>\t\t\t<td>1. Electron with <math><mi>&#160;</mi><mover accent=\"true\"><mrow><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mfrac><mrow><msub><mrow><mi>E</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mi>B</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mfrac><mover accent=\"true\"><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>&#160;</mi></math></td>\t\t\t<td>(i) <math><mover accent=\"true\"><mrow><mi>E</mi></mrow><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><msub><mrow><mi>E</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><mover accent=\"true\"><mrow><mi>z</mi></mrow><mo>^</mo></mover></math></td>\t\t\t<td>(P) <math><mi>&#160;</mi><mover accent=\"true\"><mrow><mi>B</mi></mrow><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><msub><mrow><mi>B</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><mover accent=\"true\"><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>^</mo></mover></math></td>\t\t</tr>\t\t<tr>\t\t\t<td>2. Electron with <math><mi